    "question": "One hundred chips were divided by Ian and Lyle in the ratio 4:6. What percentage of the chips did Lyle have?",
    "gold": "60",
    "answer": "The chips were divided into 4 + 6 = <<4+6=10>>10 parts.\nEach part has 100/10 = <<100/10=10>>10 chips.\nSince Lyle owns 6 parts, then he has 6 x 10 = <<6*10=60>>60 chips.\nThis is 60/100 x 100 = <<60/100*100=60>>60% of the entire chips.\n#### 60"
